/* WebGL2 renderer for the canal street and the night sky.
 *
 * The street is still generated by scene.js (same seed, same detail). On load it is baked
 * into three images: every light off, every light on, and an id map (which light owns each
 * pixel). From then on the GPU draws everything:
 *   - per pixel, lit or dark depending on how many applications have been sent
 *   - real multiply lighting from lamps, windows and portholes (instanced light pass)
 *   - moonlight relief on the brick, scaled by the real moon phase
 *   - water: the street mirrored, rippling over time, only its lights surviving
 *   - the drifting loop and the zoom (read from the svg camera every frame)
 * The sky (stars + a lit, phased moon) is a second full-page canvas.
 * The svg stays for the cyclist, the rowboat, the edge fade and clicks.
 * Without WebGL2, none of this runs and the svg version is shown as before.
 */
